  "question": {
    "text": "Rolle&#39;s theorem is not applicable for the function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo></math> in the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo></math> because"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;does not exist",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> does not exist",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is discontinuous at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> does not exist",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0032_0f2671ed16f3.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 190px;\" /></p><p>We know that the function is not differentiable at the sharp edges. Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is not differentiable at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.&nbsp; Therefore,&nbsp;Rolle&#39;s theorem is not applicable for the function</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> does not exist.</p>"
  }
